SPURS: cellSpursEventFlagWait refuses a second PPU waiter on a flag with CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR_BUSY.

Idea from Re-TeRo17/ps3recomp 2200b150f377aed7a4b89c41c2caaa61e40908d2 ("spurs: a second PPU EventFlagWait gets BUSY,
as on hardware", libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c) (MIT); hand rewrite on our tree, nothing else taken.

Problem: the event flag has one PPU wait slot (ctrl.ppuWaitMask / ppuWaitSlotAndMode / ppuPendingRecv in the 128-byte
guest struct). Real SPURS answers a PPU wait on a flag another PPU thread is blocked on with CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR_BUSY
at once, before it looks at the bits; a wait whose bits are already there never blocks and never takes the slot. RPCS3's
_cellSpursEventFlagWait does the same (BUSY when ppuWaitMask or ppuPendingRecv is set; ppuWaitMask is set only on the
blocking path; read 2026-11-19 for behaviour, nothing copied) [src:rpcs3-cellspurs]. Our HLE wait is poll-based and on
purpose writes no PPU wait slot in the guest struct (so the lifted SPU Set code takes its "no PPU waiter" path), so it
had no record of a blocked PPU waiter and a second one blocked too. Two completions landing before either waiter runs
then set the bit once, one waiter consumes it (AUTO clear) and the other sleeps for good, where the title's own code
expects the BUSY answer (Re-TeRo17 report it as a Drakengard 3 package-loader stall). Not seen in our titles; ToD and A4O
both import cellSpursEventFlagWait.

Fix (libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c): EventFlagSync (the host side table keyed by the flag's EA) gets ppu_waiting, guarded by
the sync lock. cellSpursEventFlagWait returns CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR_BUSY when it is set; the wait loop sets it just
before its first sleep (only a wait that blocks takes the slot) and clears it after the loop with the lock held again.
ef_sync_alloc zeroes it (a re-Initialize frees and reallocates the slot). cellSpursEventFlagTryWait is unchanged here
(RPCS3 refuses it too while a PPU waiter holds the slot; follow-up if a title needs it).

Test: port/rc/tests/test_spurs_eventflag_busy.c (port/rc/tests/run_spurs_eventflag_busy_test.sh, unity build of
cellSpurs.c, real threads): a satisfied wait returns at once; waiter A blocks, waiter B on the same flag gets BUSY within
500 ms and A is not disturbed; a wait on another flag is accepted; A wakes on its bit with AUTO clear; a new waiter is
accepted and woken after A left. Negative control (the tree without this patch): FAIL "second PPU waiter blocked on a
flag that already has one (expected BUSY)".

diff --git a/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c b/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
--- a/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
+++ b/libs/spurs/cellSpurs.c
@@ -104,6 +104,11 @@
     pthread_cond_t      cond;
 #endif
     int                 initialized;
+    /* R&C patch 7111: a PPU thread is blocked in cellSpursEventFlagWait on this
+     * flag (the HLE's stand-in for the kernel's ctrl.ppuWaitMask, which the
+     * poll-based wait deliberately leaves 0 in the guest struct). Guarded by
+     * the sync lock. */
+    int                 ppu_waiting;
 } EventFlagSync;
 
 static EventFlagSync s_ef_sync[MAX_EVENT_FLAGS];
@@ -146,6 +151,7 @@
     for (int i = 0; i < MAX_EVENT_FLAGS; i++) {
         if (!s_ef_sync[i].initialized) {
             s_ef_sync[i].ea = ea;
+            s_ef_sync[i].ppu_waiting = 0;   /* R&C patch 7111 */
             { extern void (*g_spu_line_commit_hook)(uint32_t);
               g_spu_line_commit_hook = ef_line_committed; }
 #ifdef _WIN32
@@ -3133,6 +3139,18 @@
 
     ef_lock(sync);
 
+    /* R&C patch 7111: one PPU waiter per flag. Real SPURS answers a PPU wait
+     * on a flag another PPU thread is blocked on (ctrl.ppuWaitMask set) with
+     * CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR_BUSY at once, before it looks at the bits; titles
+     * handle that. Letting both block loses a wakeup instead: two completions
+     * landing before either waiter runs set the bit once, one waiter consumes
+     * it (AUTO clear) and the other sleeps for good. A wait whose bits are
+     * already there never blocks, so it never marks the flag. */
+    if (sync->ppu_waiting) {
+        ef_unlock(sync);
+        return CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR_BUSY;
+    }
+
     /* Block until the requested bit pattern is satisfied in the GUEST struct
      * (BE events word at +0x00) — set by an SPU task (lifted code / taskset
      * syscall) or another PPU thread. Poll-based: ef_wait_timed ticks re-read
@@ -3160,6 +3178,7 @@
                 break;
         }
 
+        sync->ppu_waiting = 1;   /* R&C patch 7111: set under the lock before the first sleep */
         if (!ef_wait_timed(sync, 2)) {
             /* Report the stall once per second, naming what would have to run. */
             if (++waits % 500 == 0) {
@@ -3182,6 +3201,7 @@
         }
     }
 
+    sync->ppu_waiting = 0;   /* R&C patch 7111: lock held again; the flag takes a new PPU waiter */
     __atomic_sub_fetch(&s_ef_ppu_waiters, 1, __ATOMIC_SEQ_CST);
     ef_wait_stats(ea, ef_t0.QuadPart);
     /* Hand back the observed bits; consume the received ones on AUTO clear. */
